    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0470" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.00/8–449: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Missions in the American
                        Republics</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-04T02:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1949—2
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inter-Amer Peace Comite met Aug 3 at suggestion US Rep to consider gen situation
                    involving polit tensions Caribbean area. Comite unanimously agreed consideration
                    this subject desirable and ltr drafted<anchor n="1" xml:id="d286-f1"/>
                    requesting each Amer Govt for info or suggestions it considered
                        pertinent.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d286-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Comite fully realized it lacked power take any affirmative action to deal with
                    situation other than suggestion of methods that might be employed. All members
                    felt highly important obtain further info and views from govts before
                    considering any further steps.</p>
                <p>US Rep did not, as implied some press statements, suggest mtg FonMins or any other specific step beyond
                    consideration gen problem by Comite itself.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d286-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d286-f1" n="1" xml:id="d286-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d286-f2" n="2" xml:id="d286-f2-content">
                <p>Replies were received from Costa Rica, Cuba, the Dominican Republic, Guatemala,
                    Haiti, the United States, and Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d286-f3" n="3" xml:id="d286-f3-content">
                <p>In a circular telegram to Diplomatic Representatives in the American Republics,
                    August 5, not printed, the Department emphasized its lack of zeal for a meeting
                    of Foreign Ministers at that time (810.00/8–549).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
